et of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $¬P(x),$ we take all the points that belong to $U$ and do not lie in ${T}_{p},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/9a/9abb3d8964713cf893acb17f26742eed4c5c442ce813cd81ed4d5aba26968bda.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "adbddf14-3aca-50dd-80f8-4146193c91ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of Predicate's Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d659fe3-9d2f-537a-a3f9-ec8dea805d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6aab81a1af9039ff6f4ebce3fecb06ba6ad687cb6af22dcf76bd803ac4ddf940.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389769} {:answer/id #uuid "6c583e4a-009f-504e-b20e-9a141c0e2d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/41/41f32abbcc3dec501392378379bceb0d1c111ab4c458d832508f20adb42451e6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389770} {:answer/id #uuid "73c8a9e8-9d4b-5242-be0c-57b5f01c551d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/20/2066e7be5a62a804f39aa114b64884c155cb943e2a68d60711926e0a84af20cb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389771} {:answer/id #uuid "ce809fa8-0123-5b3b-8168-d09d72867788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c32eb098fff70a1650242ba2815cd8120eb6da2a7d5f3e5d2a4e44646beca6de.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389772} {:answer/id #uuid "9a837228-5d89-52a6-9b6b-b015cc560a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bb2a35ad33731bfe5f26960a518a038b21a9445e38e3647a792326e23fd105ad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a837228-5d89-52a6-9b6b-b015cc560a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bb2a35ad33731bfe5f26960a518a038b21a9445e38e3647a792326e23fd105ad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389773} :answer-field/id #uuid "40c34b2