y {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7325f028-0857-51c9-8e64-d5a4d7ff032e" :question/math-academy-id "q-177351" :question/problem "$12$ is a multiple of $4$ **and** $8$ is odd.\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $A:12\\text{ is a multiple of }4$\n\n- $B:8\\text{ is odd}$\n\nExpressed in symbolic form, our statement can be written as\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{12\\text{ is a multiple of }4}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{8\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∧B.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b14a11-e6b5-506f-9de0-45914bda798c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/40676f8a464e854ba8835ac3b7cd79b2238cd289cdbc79519dee9caf9b0ffc87.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389791} {:answer/id #uuid "1db7bc59-804b-5f29-b2e7-ed77d3651fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/097203c1cb185dbd1831bb4b4c50b0706286633ba2cee57847490e0ef467d180.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389792} {:answer/id #uuid "e265ab27-7329-5f5b-997a-8aa391a16386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e9/e9fec69a68e4d6aadee105f3c51e76360d665ec2216ab99ffe3995c92d59b1b3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389793} {:answer/id #uuid "c84fee97-b3ae-5fc1-b9ef-f9105d5a9785" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/ac1557333e74ae3877d09896257a04785015a4aea19ccb4ce5e20909110a4340.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389794} {:answer/id #uuid "e984a352-8139-54fd-a2c2-7d7278fe018c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd92a4ea28fac423f57711ebb5bfbcfefb6bbda111a50b0402a78d7fb2707a5d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db7bc59-804b-5f29-b2e7-ed77d3651fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/097203c1cb185dbd1831bb4b4c50b0706286633ba2cee57847490e0ef467d180.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389792} :answer-field/id #uuid "075f5fcb-b558-5910-a6fc-c859b6286336" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "145e0e1b-efda-5e79-8490-e4ab75074f7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-177644" :question/problem "![](images/41/418a795217017781e09ad81114e796be1da10028161432f2f4bc78ea7d9b8968.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of the predicates $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P∨Q?$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P∨Q$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∨Q}={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x,y)∨Q(x,y),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}$ or ${T}_{Q},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/09/097203c1cb185dbd1831bb4b4c50b0706286633ba2cee57847490e0ef467d180.png)\n\n**Note:** The points where the *solid* line meets the *dashed* curve belong to ${T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}$ since these points lie in ${T}_{P}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ec4788-c9fa-5856-aa79-ed932a7b324d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389798} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc1c924-ac4a-5694-9ff3-76277fe7d08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/781bd7c0c99aa965c5b20b6545e1ab76acbbc88d7698fbed1afe3e7a6d22a14c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389799} {:answer/id #uuid "ef857f1a-d365-55c1-9f94-4a0e4c46efc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1a/1ab3b9c6a9a4b9f7bb4c481770e9fbf2beec8998eda65d22418535dca31d58bc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389800} {:answer/id #uuid "88e6a03c-020e-515c-97ad-a0dbc44a2bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/efa51ca7fcb2e24c5f7a77114a7accb008696dd012d60307937c26c1039e6892.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389801} {:answer/id #uuid "8944f4c5-55a9-51e1-a1e9-7dc77668ffb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de4621c16bad151116f6c6fa4b197c6207b527bff90e5f9c857405ca3e6b135d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20ec4788-c9fa-5856-aa79-ed932a7b324d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389798} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9db75d-b8b1-5171-a35a-f70bc057c59e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4eda50f7-a585-5a86-9e62-dbc7c5c300f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-177645" :question/problem "![](images/76/761e02a7613e2d1df4722b7bf6f0a7e1d0b5e7b6dec09d205a1e72a29b8c5eb8.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of the predicates $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P∨Q?$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P∨Q$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∨Q}={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x,y)∨Q(x,y),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}$ or ${T}_{Q},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png)\n\n**Note:** The points where the *solid* line meets the *dashed* curve belong to ${T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}$ since these points lie in ${T}_{P}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c00cf5df-4240-5b04-850f-1b4b0d6f8ae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c87871c50b343792c73fc18dfe92bc2065b18ed3de1e7bb70324b8b43d027206.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389805} {:answer/id #uuid "1f633a02-8088-56db-88c2-7889ba264321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/39/39db7bc1b259b222a2365441babc3421101961ea26a7143af14b526ba7f81200.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389806} {:answer/id #uuid "6c189e68-bec8-518b-a64d-56fe2a4c4033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec0e1df36bf5d93b8cdbcc3d14cd510fbe299b929ed3d19f4d901f4461093305.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389807} {:answer/id #uuid "f10813b1-b163-59a5-a38f-0b5b4e7dded5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f90de7c6d88b187af3604912a647620fb88d4833e08fd086cf1a9daae52f331f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389808} {:answer/id #uuid "81b3b685-552f-53ef-8556-c54cf7663b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/86/8627676ae3b7bcdeff423d79d7289d1d3f9243e0cc69d4f3ac7d3e5c51141fc1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f633a02-8088-56db-88c2-7889ba264321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/39/39db7bc1b259b222a2365441babc3421101961ea26a7143af14b526ba7f81200.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389806} :answer-field/id #uuid "f376ba00-5dab-590e-a791-4441f99a66cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60baa69f-bbf2-5905-831d-ab5e879fa2f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177648" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5b/5b882f3fb0e7b44eb2df3a510260574e5c4a4d85842a9c0d65515f1a40894756.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,1]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,1),$ and $(0,1).$\n\n![](images/cb/cb530698591dbd71a8058d9faa0c60b636dc654f21e92d65ec8295aeaa67355a.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment ${0}\\times [0,1]:$\n\n![](images/70/704f8f6f0666d09bb2b8a25eab0548c3eb808e2c9d394d2ae873de35cb0112d1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b35462e3-d90d-5229-9bb7-a180bdbea833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/aa/aaa04c2578557d03dd144c27e6a5c223126830ba2a3f8288adc9239daf604e55.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389812} {:answer/id #uuid "32da30c7-4f73-5968-bd10-234d5aa6eb9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/98/98077ef737a2487f9e480b7ffd42376785c5681e2651b98e7b71abb4e645d876.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389813} {:answer/id #uuid "94b8b364-2f47-562b-be4f-8d6d5b53993c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/36b36ac05cb1054e198f2e40a2d0ffdd40e952abaa8ddf5c946a38fde946adc8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389814} {:answer/id #uuid "1da4c351-345b-51fc-b9bc-106b693a793a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4a81de1a698eedf6a636d66b68a7c62efa69d1d026a961ae97ab5ecc2ef9828d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389815} {:answer/id #uuid "f684dbe0-2990-5f82-837b-23d70335f3f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/749f4fb3a6416147cdd69c08bf806c28e2112929453bb8ae405c48452d82126b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1da4c351-345b-51fc-b9bc-106b693a793a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4a81de1a698eedf6a636d66b68a7c62efa69d1d026a961ae97ab5ecc2ef9828d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389815} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3b75ec-dbba-566e-adfa-fb7b15c6d5b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62556693-fd48-5895-851c-d4aab5200ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177650" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times {i}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times {0.5}={(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,0.5]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0,0.5)$ to the point $(0.5,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/75/7587daeaea45c5ef3449ecb676133c60bbedb7819308783bac835f3ae9c6883c.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times {i}={(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(0,i)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](images/b9/b926204a3d58b25889f1c79dd0f65c1ea990c67bc88e869004396a77970e8dd4.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/4a/4a81de1a698eedf6a636d66b68a7c62efa69d1d026a961ae97ab5ecc2ef9828d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af8829ea-eabd-5fae-9578-d03488cfc3af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/26/26e4af1684065b2127b0d9ec33632128f62a3b2b3aa772b48062ed23708b1b7d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389819} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0a9aea-b6fe-56e1-a8a9-e3ac81332f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f3d6fcce069f0b7b7918481b4cda68ba16fbb94dbf3ebe6b6841256470b84ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389820} {:answer/id #uuid "a269d017-1375-58cf-b810-de5eeec9412c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/db/db4bea7c2f08abb66318443c88a0504bbfdc3d9597b3f42a8808795ebc78b172.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389821} {:answer/id #uuid "e387bc96-400f-584b-a615-edb0551b66e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3b/3b3cefa03d71d99e4b7f3b6852ed36512d2a841a37c558034eac5c4b6870799c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389822} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb67f6a-535a-53df-a825-cfba0db7f11b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a156cbc15d6841b1d661b77c3b2cf7e6459246e20653da5e461cc6446aded4c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e387bc96-400f-584b-a615-edb0551b66e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3b/3b3cefa03d71d99e4b7f3b6852ed36512d2a841a37c558034eac5c4b6870799c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389822} :answer-field/id #uuid "6201decc-d007-5bcc-852b-b1b8b5bc7b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0ade82f-e346-52ab-87f9-cb9aa1c85b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-177651" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times {2i}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-0.5,0.5]\\times {1}={(k,1)\\,:\\,k\\in [-0.5,0.5]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(-0.5,1)$ to the point $(0.5,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/6c/6c6aafd9ea78868e953340eaab3862491d275972d690e2ceb27c213dadbcaea6.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times {2i}={(k,2i)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(-i,2i)$ to the point $(i,2i).$ \n\n![](images/02/02c8f93a25d7b510d3e238e6d4a974d6ccc2e83f3ac01fe92ce4535fbb4dce48.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/3b/3b3cefa03d71d99e4b7f3b6852ed36512d2a841a37c558034eac5c4b6870799c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d22726fc-8e6b-5e22-80c8-fbc2aa245217" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Combinations of Objects Chosen From a Group of at Least Ten"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cec59a22-5d6d-5de8-9f8a-45ef6bb808a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,957\\,920" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389826} {:answer/id #uuid "afeaf0f3-14db-58e7-8c72-651f40583589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,581\\,580" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389827} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb700f8-9524-59c1-89ab-917235da5475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,209\\,112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389828} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc04816-e879-5d68-b950-f374a65870ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,662\\,100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389829} {:answer/id #uuid "c82b7429-84d6-539e-b5c5-1835b7badc17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "750\\,020" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afeaf0f3-14db-58e7-8c72-651f40583589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,581\\,580" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389827} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c7c9200-9af1-5711-bd23-c6a6abc5a745" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4bfaea9e-ab13-55ff-a72c-f7e351269ac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-1781" :question/problem "How many different ways can a group of four be made from a room of eighty people?" :question/worked-solution "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $80$ people, so $n=80.$ We want to select $4$ of those people for each group, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different potential groups of four is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{80}{C}_{4} & =\\frac{80!}{(80-4)!\\,4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{80!}{76!4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{80\\cdot 79\\cdot 78\\cdot 77\\cdot \\cancel{76!}}{\\cancel{76!}4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{80\\cdot 79\\cdot 78\\cdot 77}{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{37\\,957\\,920}{24} \\\\  & =1\\,581\\,580.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "562c9283-48db-53e3-8e1b-90f287599846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389833} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7fa272-b6f8-590f-9c5b-65d9f9dfa430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad7fa272-b6f8-590f-9c5b-65d9f9dfa430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389834} :answer-field/id #uuid "48a24199-8fbc-5f8a-be94-b1433383cd8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff4660a1-9de3-5baa-87b3-1593351fefd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389836} {:answer/id #uuid "23d43ed5-1f81-5a25-b0c9-296027e1069f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff4660a1-9de3-5baa-87b3-1593351fefd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389836} :answer-field/id #uuid "8252abad-b399-5caf-b293-dc6a3db02c60" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389835} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf7d3285-15e0-5c92-91fa-76404ef88ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389839} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb36f52-020a-5e2f-84e1-9b8fce7b0301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf7d3285-15e0-5c92-91fa-76404ef88ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389839} :answer-field/id #uuid "790a635b-b899-57d8-88e4-a24e66556c49" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb4c15c3-7ea2-5717-b42a-a17f62554b99" :question/math-academy-id "q-178151" :question/problem "$$\n{{N\\cap Z=N}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{3\\text{ is even}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{39\\text{ is prime}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∧(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, and the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∧\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7c35604-c9f9-5077-bddc-fe9446ac45e6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Permutation Given Using Alternate Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b9a4e42-e7a4-5567-9255-266bf2684cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389842} {:answer/id #uuid "69953b2f-ea64-5f14-b941-99a9de5efb2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\,760" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389843} {:answer/id #uuid "c929f59d-0dc6-5cfb-8e4a-aa247836ca76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51\\,820" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389844} {:answer/id #uuid "2d42ded4-3af5-53fa-82c5-2863b236289e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,410" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389845} {:answer/id #uuid "b93fa934-71d5-5ac8-b9d5-0f41c3ee4142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1365" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69953b2f-ea64-5f14-b941-99a9de5efb2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\,760" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389843} :answer-field/id #uuid "730b6fd9-57b6-5a37-9f98-5104300cc371" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19bc6957-d170-5412-80aa-cd50c7d03c4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-1783" :question/problem "$P(15,4)=$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(15,4)$ means the same thing as ${}_{15}{P}_{4}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(15,4) & =\\frac{15!}{(15-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15!}{11!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot \\cancel{11!}}{\\cancel{11!}} \\\\  & =15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =32\\,760.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b93e431e-f423-58c3-b385-0ebc44999636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∧C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389849} {:answer/id #uuid "75b30760-3ca0-54ff-8ceb-b2cc1c08c3df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧C)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389850} {:answer/id #uuid "c63ca685-30ec-5396-83dc-4a59fc6f2022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∧C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389851} {:answer/id #uuid "799b5c13-10e0-566e-964e-5e0cfc8cc319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389852} {:answer/id #uuid "17631a4c-5807-5d55-9dbd-b6058cfa0a96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∨C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17631a4c-5807-5d55-9dbd-b6058cfa0a96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∨C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389853} :answer-field/id #uuid "03b6e0ac-b4b2-57d1-b911-36ad9a375e43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e23c421-01c3-5007-b397-83f3b7b7f3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-178521" :question/problem "$5$ is less than $2$ **or** odd, **or** $9$ is composite.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A:5\\text{ is less than }2$\n\n- $B:5\\text{ is odd}$\n\n- $C:9\\text{ is composite}$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $5$ is less than $2$ or odd. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{5\\text{ is less than }2}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{5\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $9$ is composite. This corresponds to $C.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{5\\text{ is less than }2\\text{ or }\\text{odd}}_{⏟}}_{A\\,∨\\,B},\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{9\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{C}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A∨B)∨C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "689292ec-bfe1-5e21-ab2b-a047513ecb14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∧(N∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389856} {:answer/id #uuid "bc45d018-7910-56be-8da2-76d78c35e672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∨(N∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389857} {:answer/id #uuid "27fc6d4d-28b6-59d1-8028-f2bf3b05def7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∨(N∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389858} {:answer/id #uuid "3773f8ac-79f2-55af-874b-fbbdbb6b2417" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N∨(M∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389859} {:answer/id #uuid "77a6628d-cb03-5e87-abe4-da1053984e7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∧(N∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "689292ec-bfe1-5e21-ab2b-a047513ecb14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∧(N∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389856} :answer-field/id #uuid "c483c35b-ded2-5ae5-a93c-e05e88583498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d98000f-e797-5b7c-906d-57b4553eddaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-178523" :question/problem "$\\pi $ is rational, **and** $2$ is less than $4$ **and** $2\\in Z.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $M:\\pi \\text{ is rational}$\n\n- $N:2\\text{ is less than }4$\n\n- $P:2\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\pi $ is rational. This corresponds to $M.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $2$ is less than $4$ and $2\\in Z.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{ is less than }4}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{2\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∧P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\pi \\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{2\\text{ is less than }4\\text{ and }2\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{N\\,∧\\,P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $M∧(N∧P).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17fd5c3d-d4c6-5f78-b262-fbc6b7209501" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Where the Extrema of a Quadratic Form Is Attained Over an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f929e6fc-859c-554c-b8d1-7edc7d26c0b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389863} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ef524e-3272-5724-9dcf-18dac71f64f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389864} {:answer/id #uuid "5908cb4e-dd22-5985-bab6-7726588673da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389865} {:answer/id #uuid "da4cfa35-5f24-5531-a00c-981216fded81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389866} {:answer/id #uuid "632432f1-e342-5b99-b90c-6df4e61f0365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "632432f1-e342-5b99-b90c-6df4e61f0365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389867} :answer-field/id #uuid "4acab487-d1e8-587d-9ab8-b10c8019f1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9517d41a-5a17-54a5-b8d2-6ea1cb7908a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-179407" :question/problem "The maximum value of $Q(x)=-{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2},$ when ${x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}=4,$ is $12.$ Find a vector $x$ at which the maximum is attained." :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n Notice that we can write the constraint equation as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}_{2}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\n This is an ellipse with semiaxes $a=2$ (along the ${x}_{1}$-axis) and $b=1$ (along the ${x}_{2}$-axis). If we introduce new variables\n\n$\\,$ ${y}_{1}=\\frac{{x}_{1}}{2}\\,$ and $\\,{y}_{2}={x}_{2},$\n\n the equation of the ellipse will transform into ${y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}=1$ or $‖y‖=1.$\n\n So, introducing a change-of-coordinate matrix \n\n \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\n we obtain that $x=Py.$ Substituting this into the expression of the quadratic form, we get\n\n \n\n$$\nQ(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax=(Py)^{T}A\\,(Py)={y}^{T}\\,({P}^{T}AP)y={Q}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\n As a result, since ${P}^{T}=P,$ the matrix of our quadratic form in new coordinates is \n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & ={P}^{T}\\,AP \\\\  & =PAP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n Now, we maximize ${Q}^{′}(y)$ when $||y||=1,$ as usual.\n\n Since we are told that the maximum value of the quadratic form is $12,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\nmax{{Q}^{′}(y)\\,|\\,‖y‖=1}={\\lambda }_{max}=12.\n$$\n\n Next, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=12:$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-12I & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{aligned}]-12[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Seeking a non-zero solution of $(B-12I)y=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\n Finally, we map this vector back to the initial coordinate  system using the change-of-coordinates matrix:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{max}} & =P{u}_{\\text{max}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f930f1e0-0d30-5aa9-b5fd-483a8a5c9a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389869} {:answer/id #uuid "cb2d7141-7e67-5310-b9fb-4911d2b63443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389870} {:answer/id #uuid "0ad9e1f0-b0b4-597f-90f2-178c494264ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389871} {:answer/id #uuid "c7a26ace-a33e-5e44-920a-ef46de209462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb2d7141-7e67-5310-b9fb-4911d2b63443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389870} :answer-field/id #uuid "95df0cdf-950e-5250-b48b-9bd36aee12ad" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d86f82c-8316-505b-b553-4fc50fd9be03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389874} {:answer/id #uuid "720661ec-d6dc-5155-a5be-6815521ba78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389875} {:answer/id #uuid "f66d2d9b-f044-5e75-9670-5c5ecd12f8f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389876} {:answer/id #uuid "d6a987de-4180-572b-8e40-3e535fcd333a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f66d2d9b-f044-5e75-9670-5c5ecd12f8f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389876} :answer-field/id #uuid "55bd5ae5-5b4f-55f6-b43c-4cad838b1cfb" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389873} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b94fd28-8321-5c2f-ac50-326bcd0107f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389879} {:answer/id #uuid "2fcd3dce-e66c-5440-9a1f-db5da4cf74c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389880} {:answer/id #uuid "116998cf-a83c-50e3-97b7-785cb04e9079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389881} {:answer/id #uuid "27ba4f93-fa01-5ecf-a013-03a1d5f5c8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b94fd28-8321-5c2f-ac50-326bcd0107f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389879} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d59c79f-c995-5031-933c-dec7cd272d96" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a284bb-2593-59dc-92b1-465a7f0a0a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389884} {:answer/id #uuid "64342057-7043-5028-8df0-d18c85d0371b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389885} {:answer/id #uuid "6a90ed9a-2c04-53a2-8e4a-43619960ede7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389886} {:answer/id #uuid "d702dec8-a8dd-55dc-b1e0-5da84d543677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a90ed9a-2c04-53a2-8e4a-43619960ede7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389886} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb98a5a9-020e-549b-8dfd-ac958381ea84" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4062f2e3-5ce2-5706-927d-0b00b91472a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389889} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb9e5ff-beef-554c-834f-f94296d153ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389890} {:answer/id #uuid "5a43bce1-48cf-500a-9710-22c0207b2693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389891} {:answer/id #uuid "12983aa2-003c-5e08-9553-fa254287b24c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389892} {:answer/id #uuid "d322c9f2-6eea-5a6c-928b-46473e30f25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389893} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6d1a27-c6c6-5b53-950b-9eaa6b2d1ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12983aa2-003c-5e08-9553-fa254287b24c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389892} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd9d9adb-106e-598c-93ae-8f50a1356364" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d5f6382-0496-52d1-a2e2-159ffe2ef26c" :question/math-academy-id "q-181129" :question/problem "![](images/d5/d550ecec3b7103c9510b6e45e738ae1385e07fa63ff2e50c54da6c17606faaec.png)\n\nDescribe the set of points shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in {-3,-2,-1},\\,y\\in {-4,-3,-2,-1}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaa5394f-664d-516c-a7ca-0034c1aac434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/17/179fea73a29a658124583602bf26485b25ba70f66ca8187c47d745f46de25e1d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389896} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7583ed-df6d-5be7-bfdd-4f5596ff6fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/89ac9e71d8152097657f0c01daecf2b894dc142db4ba27fbfadcb8ded6e9cb19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389897} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3bbeb0-b786-56a0-af4c-ce843e2f2a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b8a268a69a978e7f9a14afd83c7c14735d797d4359826ae86f84873e53635363.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389898} {:answer/id #uuid "df54159c-0862-5afe-bf76-a3155b444d65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/acccce074e5dee93bbca149c16c5f7794dce17d1cd16432d25b0132382d877f8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389899} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c9bb19-93d6-5bb3-b166-5ed944544ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0a03f883f977e67b9299d52e1572e484ed6010dc4f2555c7cbc2048f193dbc7f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb3bbeb0-b786-56a0-af4c-ce843e2f2a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b8a268a69a978e7f9a14afd83c7c14735d797d4359826ae86f84873e53635363.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389898} :answer-field/id #uuid "21c822ca-1685-5918-acdb-d7b9f7059651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2bbd8412-3c29-5dd3-ab23-10004aeed05b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181303" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=R\\times N\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a real number and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in N}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in R}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/f8/f8808e4c35775c754dab0bf328a8d129e423009e18ec5f4b962461eba2afcea2.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $2.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(x,2)\\,:\\,x\\in R}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a5/a51fe9dc5bf7c55b01f72a45d4b88bde4653f0d3da85c1231b0d54c76a6e8c81.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\times N & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $R\\times N$ as the set of horizontal lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/7a/7ae3c488e60d3dcda304649e575a7d2efc54be7262a54d0455550af420c39b68.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63212b76-4dd2-5413-b5ba-4e9195ab76e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/82f9ecf98b8b2b4e5f75b3130e8483354c93922dc3a942e271562ac1ad17438e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389903} {:answer/id #uuid "4a858bfb-ee22-5b56-9050-fa66d28f0274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e0/e0fa3e717af02a353db77ae8b357dc338c975166fb5fbe6c5c1309d1c1f511f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389904} {:answer/id #uuid "7442f1d4-b621-53b9-a885-39076816c0b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c28ba6b0da8364f4e7f157b58827384f9e138a2c0fc53558ce7ab2df2f646747.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389905} {:answer/id #uuid "281cc561-5401-5252-9068-734db096e5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/075454dae9ed36967a70537cdf3a3f59931cdd81671ff4059658d2e0df438898.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389906} {:answer/id #uuid "b42501d9-b115-5c79-8921-c1756b26a1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/2922ff5e3a32e01fbc292898c88c1d8eca8d933897d4b9d3c1694b6f5cbeb2a2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "281cc561-5401-5252-9068-734db096e5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/075454dae9ed36967a70537cdf3a3f59931cdd81671ff4059658d2e0df438898.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389906} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f377c8c-6598-5676-856c-726dc4aca072" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "734eb671-4f30-5ac2-952a-94e297467ed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-181306" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[-1,1]\\times {-1,1}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[-1,1]\\times {-1,1}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1],\\,y\\in {-1,1}}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3e/3ed05ffc58aad1a6c75e7862c1175f497fb14870e6650cc6c4ce01c3df091d8b.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/0f/0f57920b2532177b0d64ac3dc95feb6a476bb385112d736d702895862e7de2b2.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the two line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/07/075454dae9ed36967a70537cdf3a3f59931cdd81671ff4059658d2e0df438898.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Schematic for a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc1e2521-377a-583c-ae3c-a594986136a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6cceec57dbf53e768fc290d864fa770c70a6642bdc9df1309119e113241b0f34.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389910} {:answer/id #uuid "6100ffa9-8836-588a-ad6d-756450d570c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a52e05a3884e5d62ffaacc73104a4f2e61fb8013fb353c850cdb974e66224a40.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389911} {:answer/id #uuid "1d1f178a-1f6f-5167-8e63-1743c6413ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/51/518415814ddb5483e4649c95e58aa41adc68ad8722279dbf99ac4c10bca206e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389912} {:answer/id #uuid "d789365b-3b14-591a-b824-5e4aa2089860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b7/b7497f60cccce44a008c6550f356d32564c2a15e23d88f9c3764415598dc493b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389913} {:answer/id #uuid "9b455fb2-a223-572c-adf0-f70bc35f621e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d366ec9f363cf38d84c6d741491f7e218e0bedad335f6fc1f1f954f95516f196.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d1f178a-1f6f-5167-8e63-1743c6413ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/51/518415814ddb5483e4649c95e58aa41adc68ad8722279dbf99ac4c10bca206e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389912} :answer-field/id #uuid "202c18dc-b67f-5564-b56a-fe0084384a70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "393bef1a-778c-53b8-a73e-75ffc95e3405" :question/math-academy-id "q-181958" :question/problem "Which of the following is a schematic of the Cartesian product $A\\times B$ for $A={p,q}$ and $B={w,z}?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $B$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](images/6b/6baae52e45d00d31eac732a23be655b648765c27cfcdc667c511b176d5bbbc88.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B.$\n\nOur completed $A\\times B$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](images/38/38e9d12b0c09ae066149d95235a6918712214edc147c57775da2d880b584cb9e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c52fa43-923f-576a-ba23-dee22206f178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9adb78f087651508a43514756abbc45170766d6bb14a069053c4bf71e78e0a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389917} {:answer/id #uuid "ae96fe3d-4eb2-5715-aab5-91382649a4ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d42f10aac16e2c7405fbf158dacb1b46137cc03800f8660d0ff4cfe11c9edc63.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389918} {:answer/id #uuid "2db12bff-09e6-5312-965d-054d7f6b4fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389919} {:answer/id #uuid "6f56907b-5366-5f06-9fae-bd37aae2b8cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9b/9b6a2c5b3c9fdded8d615980df00228e2637515af0a23f62ae58b891bec3e3e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389920} {:answer/id #uuid "5924e649-be02-5520-9d5e-94f6d2c07e3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a1b02e904c1df760f47d623d3ff17538c284d7ef6125b786165113a383c79c3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db12bff-09e6-5312-965d-054d7f6b4fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389919} :answer-field/id #uuid "afa6976a-3c32-54c7-bedf-912fa5e61648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9854e016-8489-5582-ad5c-ffa3a5b6e5ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-181959" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times Z\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in Z}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any integer number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/17/179fdaa3921cb29f2d25ff97bce262fd13fb2ff591c12e97a33953e95967f6fc.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/73/7399e42988df8a809013393d8873b6a6e5f60b64c0419eadd7bb3c334eb410d6.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $N\\times Z$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/16/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1204bd88-b470-5b91-b7c2-a8d4ad537898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/463ae2387423a48dd557af8cfd9b01b6bc08b95f1b3c2f337c6b0c53d3731fa2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389924} {:answer/id #uuid "60caae02-3071-514b-9258-9f96b6664d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389925} {:answer/id #uuid "746ae67c-caa3-593c-9e3f-51831b036f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389926} {:answer/id #uuid "c89a44bf-6d27-578e-9136-6babbb95e931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f28e6f8c8e6e9fa13b5285e25e5460d26548ffd9d71077d1c6073e6c4c743a1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389927} {:answer/id #uuid "51564c2b-bcad-5e6e-9c34-dbd7a16d3a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/5888cf137eea674995b4c9cc37285b4130df5de3a2a2fa63b1b5b195910526c1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "746ae67c-caa3-593c-9e3f-51831b036f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389926} :answer-field/id #uuid "c241a74d-c7f4-5b96-a451-f6a50f08f04a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bae802a-d591-53eb-b628-21b012d03cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-181968" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={Z}^{-}\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={Z}^{-}\\times N\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a negative integer and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/8e/8e6816767cd2010fca1b8991ed9c5e0c42d3a6d6466d78025534bc8362a174b9.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}={(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/4d/4d0fe261e790520e6a8786e6f024d5b9cb7cd54c18242103a1f4b77f09653abc.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-5},{S}_{-4},{S}_{-3}$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…{S}_{-4}\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1} \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in {Z}^{-}}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${Z}^{-}\\times N$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72d6c485-e050-55c8-9679-fd6d97aa00e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/96/96a29779da824d7d2dc7b6d4f2b9c781a4a593b58e44f491724221c77888e3e3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389931} {:answer/id #uuid "08a4e04e-4888-5403-95d8-f078acf2c991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e5b130683075dd04e4b5129065d32b4d75b3dabfaff0b05b90de858b5e0f2961.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389932} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e8e5e1-7a36-52d6-b8df-aa671398b7a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389933} {:answer/id #uuid "66761d80-0b06-5258-89e9-adc40f67af90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/288ca0010ecc1fada05a67637b583a6e86b7f805d4e272e91563a13c18fc164a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389934} {:answer/id #uuid "09687f1b-acf3-52b9-85d2-f72a782bfbfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/3332464bdc0583c6ce99bf126805abaf57461e67aee6bdf12c95e11042baf9c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e8e5e1-7a36-52d6-b8df-aa671398b7a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389933} :answer-field/id #uuid "46ec56ed-6fc0-52ed-aa83-998bc8081175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c70aae50-ffb5-59f2-930c-cbbe5d9bb642" :question/math-academy-id "q-181985" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[-1,0]\\times [-1,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=[-1,0]\\times [-1,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,0],\\,y\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/c9/c93f3ad399b88ccbaac990f8f73e93cfdcb1192f52b9b12f2d3ce178776fa13b.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in [-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in [-1,0],$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,-1)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/65/6557201d202a401a92ee37c9a69eab9ab6ab87c6342dbb9d2afebae30141346f.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I=[-1,0]:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf363eee-2621-5129-b8f3-366db0513b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/00/00214f8393d37e387c8d34ca2cf3a203bc59ed02243d8d1d5f66f2f7c88b129c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389938} {:answer/id #uuid "91ac1a23-682b-5c58-9824-a4ea069b0418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d8/d8d11fb28834722dddf42c232b9734a52a0d0d438b8aea9b015f4d36d87d40e6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389939} {:answer/id #uuid "f72c4674-dce2-5a79-ae01-41e6c3b8e8ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/16a277a008245ef5296a55b00a7ce45cf52b5fdd008e088ad43437f6949c4435.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389940} {:answer/id #uuid "e221f413-5882-56d9-8c26-c8e08bb83d5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/47/47b6926a31ad68d13c7e18a26d97ec6c2d173f10756e50c2e059b5dce60f876c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389941} {:answer/id #uuid "ace45802-edd9-5dcf-8997-b0c6336b668d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6f/6fc81e487503ce86d3bf5366e57db087484e8bd1e8bafd52738c65e8e173c387.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ace45802-edd9-5dcf-8997-b0c6336b668d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6f/6fc81e487503ce86d3bf5366e57db087484e8bd1e8bafd52738c65e8e173c387.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389942} :answer-field/id #uuid "c16ed38f-9c2a-5692-bc66-dd955e73e0e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06dc01d3-636a-5a37-9129-21c0ede89387" :question/math-academy-id "q-181986" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times [-1,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times [-1,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/58/588f2574b1aaf0e96895816ca34bd9c6900a9b13342f44bd4104ad2bf4270bf5.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,-1)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/84/8458978c2766d899b03149de53739650932875d6463c25dd3bbde99bc6a71ea7.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $R,$ these line segments sweep the following bar that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/6f/6fc81e487503ce86d3bf5366e57db087484e8bd1e8bafd52738c65e8e173c387.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb27ab3a-0ca0-5e64-94ce-24a393d86f64" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3006cc57-23ed-5004-88ec-62c3c6d5c9b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389944} {:answer/id #uuid "67da65ee-b672-57bc-9363-68a3203cd2f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67da65ee-b672-57bc-9363-68a3203cd2f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389945} :answer-field/id #uuid "30b61f6a-e8a2-5c6b-89f6-69c1a368b127" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} 