xt{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for $¬Q,$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column for $Q.$ \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $P∨¬Q.$ Remember that $P∨¬Q$ is true if either $P$ is true or $¬Q$ is true. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $¬(P∨¬Q),$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column $P∧¬Q.$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb27ab3a-0ca0-5e64-94ce-24a393d86f64" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59d8a1f3-07c5-58e7-85f4-8fa8d1ab728c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389996} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a410e1-d814-57ae-958a-499c29d236d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389997}] :answer-field/correct 