\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $P⇔Q$ is true if $P⇒Q$ **and** $Q⇒P.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $P⇔Q$ is true if $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add columns for $¬Y$ and $¬Y∨X:$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬Y\\,$ | $\\,¬Y∨X\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $X⇔(¬Y∨X):$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬Y\\,$ | $\\,¬Y∨X\\,$ | $\\,X⇔(¬Y∨X)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0936217d-66d2-5360-b88b-a30683720415" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Disjunctive Statements as Conditionals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb4ad52e-c1dd-5079-bf6f-6f08096788a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you water the plants, they won't grow." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057290} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c04a1f-1007-562d-a24a-d4e9da7a0948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you don't water the plants, they will grow." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057291} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b08f6a-2a82-5bb6-847d-d9e21319234a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Water the plants, and they will grow." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057292} 