th} :answer/value "{k}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390048} {:answer/id #uuid "98194006-f420-5495-a840-bb74546c42b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{k}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390049} {:answer/id #uuid "3af8c2f5-16a9-5732-b8e6-073cb7260017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af8c2f5-16a9-5732-b8e6-073cb7260017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390050} :answer-field/id #uuid "969dc866-6e47-5f45-8585-83cb6bbcdc20" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390047} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d155cb15-239d-5021-8a8d-d4e6643143dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390052} {:answer/id #uuid "825d631b-3499-5c16-a4f4-ec6350e86ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390053} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad9ffe0-dda1-57f0-b1bb-e4593a0140ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d155cb15-239d-5021-8a8d-d4e6643143dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390052} :answer-field/id #uuid "480d6806-6a60-56a6-8520-74a28aa781fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390051} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "337f5334-3b70-52fb-8899-83b2c6a56490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390056} {:answer/id #uuid "35add291-1ecb-532a-9fd9-c639bcafd7e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{k}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390057} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce65a06-b4f6-57f9-887f-31c79533648a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2k-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390058} {:answer/id #uuid "60801a72-d2b0-5d27-9f14-619700a204e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35add291-1ecb-532a-9fd9-c639bcafd7e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{k}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390057} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b2cb25-2dc6-5e74-b507-38555504293d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3125843-132f-5239-ae60-dab17f982d0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-182623" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to prove the following statement using mathematical induction:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(2i-1)={n}^{2}\n$$\n\nA proof template is outlined below. Fill in the missing statements.\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{1}(2i-1)={{field-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=$ {{field-2}}, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}(2i-1)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{k+1}(2i-1)={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(2i-1)={n}^{2}$ for all $n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To prove a statement using induction, we use the following framework:\n\n- **Step 1**: Base Case\n\n- **Step 2**: Inductive Hypothesis\n\n- **Step 3**: Inductive Step\n\n- **Step 4**: Conclusion\n\nIn this case, the general statement $P(n)$ we're required to prove is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(2i-1)={n}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe start by proving the so-called **base case,** $P(1).$ To do this, we substitute $n=1$ into both the left-hand side and right-hand side. \n\nIn our case, this gives the following:\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{1}(2i-1)={1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProving that the base case is true is usually straightforward. We simply calculate the left-hand and right-hand sides independently and show they're equal.\n\nNext, we write down our **inductive hypothesis**. We assume that $P(k)$ is true for some $n=k\\ge 1.$ To do this, we simply replace $n$ with $k$ in our original statement $P(n).$ \n\nIn our case, this gives the following:\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=k\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}(2i-1)={k}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDue to the base case, we already *know* that the statement is true for *some* value of $k,$ namely $k=1,$ so this assumption is valid. \n\nThen, we move onto the **inductive step**: We must show that $P(k)⇒P(k+1).$ We start by writing down $P(k+1).$ \n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{k+1}(2i-1)=(k+1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe inductive step is where most of the work lies. The idea is to rewrite the left-hand side of this equation *using the inductive hypothesis* and apply algebraic techniques to show that this equals the right-hand side.\n\nOnce we've shown that $P(k)⇒P(k+1),$ the proof is complete, and we state our **conclusion**.\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(2i-1)={n}^{2}$ for all $n\\ge 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a188d81-1b50-5fa0-a400-c6a11b2a8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Proof Template"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca59cf6b-5af1-56f6-8416-97751d054b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k(k+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390061} {:answer/id #uuid "49071f42-51a0-5181-97fe-3dbe0f48a66d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k(k+1)(k+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390062} {:answer/id #uuid "0a76319f-