b/id #edb/ref 17592186390181} {:answer/id #uuid "088fb8e1-80c8-5b96-9fd5-7e059d4a9db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "088fb8e1-80c8-5b96-9fd5-7e059d4a9db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390182} :answer-field/id #uuid "a223d6ba-7747-5202-9cbc-db253e2e4893" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55adfa30-bde9-5dd7-8854-b990477f8d63" :question/math-academy-id "q-183325" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={5,6,7,...,50}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS={x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers between $5$ and $50$ (including $5$ and $50$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $4<x<51.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,4<x<51},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,4<x<51}.\n$$"}]}
